.4471 35.0256 21.9579 35.0823L9.16336 36.8374C8.65535 36.9129 8.22259 36.4788 8.29785 35.9693L10.0477 23.136C10.1041 22.6642 10.3299 22.2113 10.6686 21.8905V21.8716Z\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M26.0786 6.45288L38.6285 19.0219\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M32.0432 13.0204L18.2703 26.8162\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M10.292 22.3622C13.3777 23.0227 16.1248 24.608 18.2509 26.8161C20.3959 29.0053 21.8823 31.8172 22.428 34.9501\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.50562 7.94373H11.5342\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 2.24432H16.3691\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M1.73071 13.6622H7.77047\" stroke=\"var(--meadow-accent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.14929\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</span> Notes</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-8578-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-8578-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"8578\" data-servings=\"12\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">12</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Mini croissants</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Store-bought or homemade</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"2\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Assorted fillings</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Choose from ham, cheese, jam, or chocolate spread</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"3\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For brushing</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"4\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Fresh fruit garnish</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Berries or grapes</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"5\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Fresh herbs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional, for garnish</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-8578-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8578\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking tray&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For warming the croissants</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-8578-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-8578-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8578\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8578-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat your oven to 175°C (350°F). This will ensure your croissants warm up perfectly!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8578-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Arrange the mini croissants on a baking tray. Warm them in the oven for 5–7 minutes until they are lightly golden. Keep an eye on them!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8578-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Remove the croissants from the oven and let them cool slightly. Slice each croissant horizontally, but don’t cut all the way through!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8578-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Spread butter or your favorite filling on the bottom halves. Layer with ham and cheese or jam and chocolate spread, depending on your taste!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8578-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Close the croissants gently and arrange them on a large platter. Make it look inviting!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8578-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Garnish your platter with fresh fruit and herbs for a pop of color. Serve immediately and enjoy the smiles!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-8578-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>8g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbohydrates</td>\n<td>18g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s what you&#8217;ll need to create a delightful Mini <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croissant\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Croissant </a>Platter!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Charming-Mini-Croissant-Platter.webp\" alt=\"A visually appealing mini croissant platter with assorted fillings and garnished with fresh fruits and herbs.\" class=\"wp-image-8576\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Charming-Mini-Croissant-Platter.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Charming-Mini-Croissant-Platter-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Mini croissants</strong> – 12 pieces, store-bought or homemade</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Assorted fillings</strong> – 2 cups, choose from ham, cheese, jam, or chocolate spread</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Butter</strong> – 2 tablespoons, for brushing</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh fruit garnish</strong> – 1 cup, berries or grapes</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh herbs</strong> – optional, for garnish</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-mini-croissant-platter\"><strong>How to Make Mini Croissant Platter</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful Mini Croissant Platter is perfect for any gathering! With a preparation time of 10 minutes, a cooking time of 5–7 minutes, and a little extra time for cooling, you’ll have a delicious appetizer ready in no time!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Mini-Croissant-Platter-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual guide to preparing a mini croissant platter, showcasing the warming, slicing, filling, and garnishing process.\" class=\"wp-image-8577\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Mini-Croissant-Platter-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Mini-Croissant-Platter-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 175°C (350°F). This will ensure your croissants warm up perfectly!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Warm the Croissants</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Arrange the mini croissants on a baking tray. Warm them in the oven for 5–7 minutes until they are lightly golden. Keep an eye on them!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Cool and Slice</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the croissants from the oven and let them cool slightly. Slice each croissant horizontally, but don’t cut all the way through!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add Fillings</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Spread butter or your favorite filling on the bottom halves. Layer with ham and cheese or jam and chocolate spread, depending on your taste!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Close and Arrange</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Close the croissants gently and arrange them on a large platter. Make it look inviting!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Garnish your platter with fresh fruit and herbs for a pop of color. Serve immediately and enjoy the smiles!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Appetizer / Snacks</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>French</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>7 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>17 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm and fresh with assorted fillings!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-mini-croissant-platter\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Mini Croissant Platter</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose a variety of fillings for a colorful platter.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Preheat your oven for perfectly flaky croissants.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brush with egg wash for a golden finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Assemble just before serving to maintain freshness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with dips like hummus or tzatziki for added flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-mini-croissant-platter\"><strong>How to Serve this Mini Croissant Platter</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pair with a variety of dips like hummus, tzatziki, or a creamy spinach dip.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside fresh fruit like berries, grapes, or sliced melons for a refreshing contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include a selection of cheeses such as brie, cheddar, and goat cheese for a gourmet touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer a mix of sweet and savory fillings, like chocolate spread, almond paste, or herbed cream cheese.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with fresh herbs like basil or parsley for a pop of color and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Set out small bowls of nuts or seeds for an added crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Complement with a selection of herbal teas or refreshing lemonade for a delightful beverage pairing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can prepare and store your mini croissant platter for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Mini Croissant Platter Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Place leftovers in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Separate layers with parchment paper to prevent sticking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Mini Croissant Platter</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap individual croissants in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped croissants in a freezer-safe bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Mini Croissant Platter</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place croissants on a baking sheet.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat for 10-15 minutes until warm and flaky.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For frozen croissants, add an extra 5 minutes to the heating time.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How to cut mini croissants for sandwiches?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To cut mini croissants for sandwiches, simply slice them in half horizontally using a serrated knife. This will create a perfect pocket for your fillings. Be gentle to avoid squishing the flaky layers, and you can also use a spread like cream cheese or butter to help hold the sandwich together!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How many people does a Costco croissant platter feed?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A Costco croissant platter typically feeds about 12 to 16 people, depending on the size of the croissants and how many other appetizers are being served. If you’re planning a larger gathering, consider adding a few extra platters or sides to ensure everyone is satisfied!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Does Costco have mini croissants?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Costco does offer mini croissants! They are often available in the bakery section and are perfect for parties or brunches. If you can’t find them, you can also make your own mini croissants at home using puff pastry for a delicious alternative!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How much chicken salad for 40 mini croissants?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>For 40 mini croissants, you would typically need about 5 to 6 cups of chicken salad. This amount allows for a generous filling in each croissant, ensuring that your guests enjoy a satisfying bite. Adjust the quantity based on your guests&#8217; appetites and any other dishes you may be serving!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to try this Mini Croissant Platter as we are! It’s a delightful, easy-to-make treat that’s perfect for any gathering. Picture the smiles on your friends&#8217; faces as they savor each flaky bite. So gather your ingredients, roll up your sleeves, and enjoy the simple joy of creating something delicious!</p>\n",
